---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import summary from '../data/summary.json';
---
<Base description="Search hospital-published cash prices and insurance-negotiated rates by treatment, city and insurer.">
<section class="search-hero">
 <span class="pill">Hospital prices, without the guesswork</span>
 <h1>What will it cost?</h1>
 <p class="sub">A treatment. A city. Your insurance, if you have it.</p>
 <form action="/explore" class="search-form"><label class="sr-only" for="q">Search treatment, city and insurance</label><input id="q" name="q" type="search" autofocus placeholder="MRI Austin or blood work NYC Aetna" required/><button>Search prices <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></form>
 <div class="examples"><a href="/explore?q=MRI%20Austin">MRI Austin</a><a href="/explore?q=blood%20work%20Miami">Blood work Miami</a><a href="/explore?q=MRI%20Aetna">MRI Aetna</a></div>
 <p class="muted">Published rates, not your final bill. No account. No personal health details needed.</p>
</section>
<section class="coverage"><div><strong>{summary.providers}</strong><span>primary-source files parsed</span></div><div><strong>{summary.cities}</strong><span>cities with prices</span></div><div><strong>{summary.rows.toLocaleString()}</strong><span>hospital / treatment records</span></div></section>
<section class="card" style="margin:36px 0"><h2 style="margin-top:0">Explore the dataset</h2><p class="sub">Filter by hospital, city, treatment and insurer. Inspect the source behind every price or download the data.</p><p style="margin-top:16px"><a class="button" href="/explore">Open data explorer →</a> <a style="margin-left:16px" href="/about-data">Coverage & methodology</a></p></section>
<p class="muted">Building nationwide coverage. The discovery registry contains {summary.registry_locations} locations, but only the successfully parsed files above are searchable. A daily refresh job is being tested; individual source dates remain visible. We have not yet reached thousands of hospitals.</p>
</Base>
